<title>USA: Cardiothoracic sets shareholder rights.</title>
<headline>Cardiothoracic sets shareholder rights.</headline>
<dateline>CUPERTINO, Calif. 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>CardioThoracic Systems said it declared a dividend distribution of one preferred share purchase right on each outstanding share of the Company's Common Stock.</p>
<p>Each right will entitle the holder to buy one one-thousandth of one share of the Company's Series A Participating Preferred Stock at an exercise price of $150.</p>
<p>The rights would be exercisable following the 10th day after a person or group announced the acquisition of 15 percent or more of the company's stock or started a tender offer, the consummation of which would result in ownership of 15 percent or more.</p>
</text>
